  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "gs_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -404
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Gradient fills and masks\n\nGradient Fill paints shapes with a linear, radial or conic gradient through a colour spread.\n\n• Sky: linear, in canvas units, top to bottom.\n• Sun: linear in shape units (-1..1 across its own box).\n• Stripes: a hard-edged gradient (positions 0, 0.6, 0.6, 1) repeated every 26 px, sliding down. It masks the sun by luminance: white shows, black hides. The plain rect keeps the top half whole.\n• Ring: a conic gradient on the stroke, turning.\n\nFlip `invert` on the Mask, or try mode `alpha`.",
        "width": 440,
        "height": 340
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Gradient fills and masks\n\nGradient Fill paints shapes with a linear, radial or conic gradient through a colour spread.\n\n• Sky: linear, in canvas units, top to bottom.\n• Sun: linear in shape units (-1..1 across its own box).\n• Stripes: a hard-edged gradient (positions 0, 0.6, 0.6, 1) repeated every 26 px, sliding down. It masks the sun by luminance: white shows, black hides. The plain rect keeps the top half whole.\n• Ring: a conic gradient on the stroke, turning.\n\nFlip `invert` on the Mask, or try mode `alpha`.",
        "width": 440,
        "height": 340
      }
    },
